  "title": "sha2 0.10 → 0.11 in the osf crate",
  "summary": "Bumps the `sha2` dependency of the `osf` crate from 0.10 to 0.11 and lets Cargo re-resolve the RustCrypto hash stack underneath it. The 0.11 line moves off `generic-array` onto `hybrid-array`, so `digest` jumps to 0.11, `crypto-common` to 0.2, `block-buffer` to 0.12 and `cpufeatures` to 0.3, while `generic-array` and its `version_check` helper drop out of the lockfile entirely and `const-oid` and `hybrid-array` appear. No source file changes: the crate's own hashing call sites are untouched, so the blast radius is the dependency graph and whatever consumes the digest types across the crate boundary.",
